# Alex Tait wrote the initial drawsvg-based package this grew out of and is
# credited in the README and the paper's acknowledgments; the released code is
# the author's own work. ORCID is recorded below.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use optodraw in your research, teaching, or content, please cite it
  using the metadata below.
title: "optodraw: Unified 2D/3D Authoring of Free-Space Optical Setups and Photonic Integrated Circuits"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Prosper Dellah
    family-names: Allo
    affiliation: "ACCELUMA"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0005-2027-5794"
version: 0.10.0
license: BSD-3-Clause
keywords:
  - optics
  - photonics
  - photonic integrated circuits
  - scientific visualization
  - diagrams
  - GDSII
abstract: >-
  optodraw is an open-source Python package and browser editor in which a
  single declarative scene description of an optical setup renders to
  publication SVG/TikZ, interactive 3D, animation, and GLB — spanning
  free-space optics, bench instruments, and photonic integrated circuits,
  including GDSII import with foundry layer stacks and mixed bench-and-chip
  scenes.
